{"test":"text:nat_en.txt","n_prompt":113,"pp_s":16.069,"pp_ts":7.0322,"n_gen":128,"tg_ts":4.6696,"tg_total_ts":4.6594,"gen":"The storm came in three waves. The first was a wall of water that lifted the boat from its moorings and hurled it against the rocks. The second wave was the wind, which howled through the lighthouse and sent the door slamming open and shut. The third wave was the sea itself, which rose and rose until it was lapping at the base of the tower. The lighthouse keeper stood at the window, watching the sea take the boat, and then he heard the sound of the bell. It was the old bell from the chapel, the one that had not been rung in years, and it was ringing"}
